            "notes": "Most steps in a 500-step simulation are incremental — state barely changes. Only inflection points (wildcards, threshold crossings, phase transitions) need full agent reasoning. Routine steps could use deterministic updates, interpolation, or a cheaper/faster model. Reduces LLM calls by 10-50x without losing trajectory quality at critical moments."
        },
